WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.088
Here are the risks the book
names, in three groups.

2
00:00:03.088 --> 00:00:07.889
Scope: instances found late, cluster
instances that can't take Entra logins,

3
00:00:07.889 --> 00:00:10.987
and applications that
hold their instance back.

4
00:00:10.987 --> 00:00:14.421
Sequence: engine work held up
waiting for Windows sign-in,

5
00:00:14.421 --> 00:00:18.293
the old certificate authority
retired before its replacement,

6
00:00:18.293 --> 00:00:21.288
and migration still running
when the block lands.

7
00:00:21.288 --> 00:00:25.578
Control: Azure roles that can
quietly turn SQL logins back on,

8
00:00:25.578 --> 00:00:30.126
and one server identity shared by
every application on the host.

9
00:00:30.126 --> 00:00:34.578
The decision: every residual risk
goes in the exception registry,

10
00:00:34.578 --> 00:00:39.937
with a control, an owner and an end date,
and the authorizing official accepts it.

11
00:00:39.937 --> 00:00:41.230
One last question.
